id: pm-vcs-b7cb
title: "Phase 6: scale"
description: "A loose object per blob and a full closure walk per operation are correct and simple, and they stop being adequate at a hundred thousand objects. This phase adds packed object storage, a reachability index, shallow and partial history, and garbage collection that can never remove an object the operation log still needs for undo."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:25.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:27.981Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Packed storage round-trips every object kind bit-for-bit; a reachability index answers ancestry without walking the full graph; a shallow clone can be deepened; garbage collection provably retains everything reachable from any ref or any operation-log entry
